    "chunk_size_bytes": 2110,
    "chunk_text": "Number of Courtrooms Chief Appellate High Courts\n\n22 23\n\nCommercial High Courts\n\n01 05\n\nPermanent Trial-at-Bar High Courts\n\n02 02\n\nPermanent Trial-at-Bar High Courts\n\n02 02\n\nProvincial High Courts\n\n34 48\n\nTotal 61 80\n\nIn addition, the Ministry of Justice and National Integration submitted a plan for\n\n801 802\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc2\u0dab \u0db1\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf ]\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf ]\n\n2026 \u0d94\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc1\u0dad\u0ddd\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 09\n\nincreasing the number of courts and a plan for improving the infrastructure required for that purpose on 12.02.2021, and Cabinet approval was granted on 01.03.2021. Details are given in Annexes 01* to 06*. (Refer Annexes 1 to 6 in Sinhala.)\n\nHowever, due to the economic crisis experienced in the country, infrastructure provision projects were delayed. Our Government has provided the funds required to implement these projects and is also taking steps to resolve contractual and administrative issues. Nevertheless, the shortage of engineering and technical officers has become a major challenge in this regard. Accordingly, our Government is commencing these projects systematically and 14 new construction projects are scheduled to commence in 2027. However, as the provision of infrastructure requires a certain period of time, the number of High Courts hearing criminal cases in Colombo was increased from eight to 11 by using alternative arrangements. Three courts were allocated for the expeditious disposal of bribery cases. In addition, permanent trial-at-bar courts and two regular trial-at-bar courts were established. An additional Civil Appellate High Court and a Commercial High Court have also been established.\n\nFurthermore, plans are underway to provide necessary infrastructure to establish High Courts in rented buildings on an urgent basis in locations with heavy case backlogs. Priority, under this plan, has been assigned to the following High Courts:\n\nProposed High\n\nCourt\n\nNumber of\n\nPending\n\nCases 01 Negombo 1,414\n\n02 Galle 1,678\n\n03 Kurunegala 1,819\n\n04 Matara 1,372\n\n05 Kalutara 1,078\n\n06 Kandy - currently has two courtrooms\n\n2,026"
