    "chunk_text": "(iii) Only traditional medical practitioners participate in these Conservation Councils, and only the Community Health Medical Officer - CMO - participates as the convener. (b) (i) Until 2019, applications for the registration of traditional medical students were forwarded to the Ayurveda Medical Council with the approval of the Divisional Secretary, based on the recommendations of the Conservation Council and the Grama Niladhari. However, from 2019 onwards, the Ayurveda Medical Council arranged to obtain recommendations relating to the registration of medical students from the Ayurveda Community Health Medical Officer - CMO - instead of obtaining them from the Divisional Secretary, Grama Niladhari and Conservation Councils. Accordingly, recommendations for the registration of traditional medical students are no longer provided through the Conservation Councils. Therefore, the number of obtaining membership of the Conservation Councils by traditional medical students remains low. (ii) Indicated in the Annex*. (Please refer to the Annex in Sinhala.)\n\n(c) (i) 1. Attanagalla - 01 22.Mawanella\n\n2. Attanagalla - 02 23.Medawachchiya\n\n3. Ampara 24.Mihintale\n\n4. Aranayaka 25.Mirigama\n\n5. Embilipitiya - 01 26.Morawewa\n\n6. Embilipitiya - 02 27.Rajanganaya\n\n7. Ella 28.Rathgama\n\n8. Ehetuwewa 29.Lankapura\n\n9. Eheliyagoda 30.Lahugala\n\n10. Kantale 31.Vavuniya - 01\n\n11. Kebithigollewa 32.Vavuniya - 02\n\n12. Kelaniya 33.Vakarai\n\n13. Sevenagala 34.Welikanda\n\n14. Galenbindunuwewa 35.Welipitiya\n\n15. Galnewa 36.Siyambalanduwa\n\n16. Thihagoda 37.Hanguranketha\n\n17. Dimbulagala 38.Hingurakgoda\n\n18. Palugaswewa 39.Horowpathana\n\n19. Pallepola 40.Thanamalwila\n\n20. Mahaoya 41.Nikaweratiya\n\n21. Mahiyanganaya\n\n(ii) Provisions have not been allocated within the past five years for the \"Hela Gedara\" Project.\n\n(d) Does not arise.\n\n1003 1004\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0db4\u0dd4\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dad\u0