    "chunk_size_bytes": 2287,
    "chunk_text": "6. What assumptions underpin the Government\u2019s assessment of the conflict\u2019s remaining duration? Will you table three, six and twelve-month scenarios, covering oil prices, financing gaps, reserves, debt service and contingency triggers?\n\n8. Beyond completing the existing IMF programme, has a successor arrangement been requested or discussed? What financing, conditionality, social protection and debt sustainability terms are being considered?\n\nWe have been mentioning that going to the IMF is unpalatable. But, once you declare yourself bankrupt, like what happened on the 12th of April, 2022, to come out of it, you need to hold the hand of the IMF. That four-year Programme will come to an end in March, 2027. So, there must be a successor programme and we want to know what it is. That is necessary to take the country to a stable tomorrow. So, it is in order to ensure that it happens and for the benefit of the country that we are asking the IMF programme to be continued.\n\n9. Given these risks, would securing a successor IMF programme better insulate Sri Lanka against prolonged external shocks? If not, what demonstrably more beneficial alternatives can provide comparable financing, credibility and protection? Will the Government table its comparative assessment, identify its preferred option and implementation timetable and report quarterly to Parliament on financing, delivery, outcomes and risks?\n\nThank you, Sir.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf 2\u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2\u0dba\u0dca\u0dad \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) Hon. Speaker, there are nine questions, and information has to be collected from different departments and units, though it had been referred to the Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development. Therefore, I kindly request for time to answer the Question.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Speaker) \u0d85 \u0daf\u0dc0\u0dba\u0daf\u0dcf\u0dba\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dd9\u0dda\u0dba\u0db1.\u0dbb\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Sir, I rise to a point of Order.\n\n1237 1238"
