    "chunk_text": "Now, you could see the HSBC leaving. That was something I did when I was the Minister of Trade, Commerce and Consumer Affairs. We went to UK and got these 4,000 seats. Donnelley, which is a US company, is going out of the country. Hon. Minister, I would like you to emphasize as to how we could protect investments in this country. Do not let any investments go out. I do not want to dampen the spirits, but prefer any investment in the country to be retained rather than no investments coming in. But, I do not think a conducive climate is being created by you all in order to ensure that FDIs come in.\n\n1243 1244\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dad\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dbb(\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc2\u0db1)\u0dbb\u0d85\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbb\u0dca\u200d\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dbb \u0dc0\u0daf]\n\n2026 \u0d94\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dc0\u0ddd\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc2\u0dbb22\n\nthis. But, in order to ensure that, we must have policies that are perdurable. Now, when we have a region with an absolutely profitable environment, we cannot let the country to lose out in the future. So, please ensure that we get together and forget the colourization of politics. We must build a strong economy that would be able to carry through upto April, 2028, when we have got to pay our debts on our own. The world is in a financial turbulence; you do not know what is going to happen next in the Middle East. So, if you all do not protect the dollars in hand, you are going to have a tough time. Not only you all, but the whole country, and that is why we are concerned about this.\n\nHon. Minister, I would greatly appreciate if these answers are not colorized. Whether we are on that side or you all are on this side, it is the same. But, we would like to see more purposefulness in the answers given. That is the requirement.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf 2\u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2\u0dba\u0dca\u0dad \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) Hon. Member, thank you very much for the comments. Whatever points that you just highlighted could be considered in decision-making, wherever relevant and appropriate."
